.TH UPTRKEYS 1
.SH NAME
uptrkeys \- kernel-level mouse keys for X11 and Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uptrkeys
.RB [ \-d | \-\-debug ]
.RB [ \-dd | \-\-trace ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uptrkeys
reads physical keyboard devices via Linux
.B evdev
and synthesizes virtual keyboard and pointer events via
.B uinput
across both X11 and Wayland.
.P
When the prefix key (physical
.BR CapsLock
by default) is not held, keys are forwarded transparently. Holding the prefix
key activates pointer mode, mapping keys to smooth pointer motion,
high-resolution and discrete scrolling, speed multipliers, and mouse buttons
while still passing through non-internal modifiers (such as Super or right-side
modifiers) so modifier-plus-mouse combinations work like a physical mouse.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug, \-\-verbose
Log device grabs/unplugs, key routing, pointer mode transitions, and button emissions to stderr.
.TP
.B \-dd, \-\-trace
Also log skipped /dev/input devices, key repeats, and every motion/scroll tick.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit
.I config.h
(copied from
.I config.def.h
on build) and recompile with
.BR make .
